Subject: [PATCH 15/17] docs(mcp): describe the atomic-write and batch patterns

Add docs/atomic-and-batch-tools.md, a design note for the patterns
behind the new tools, written to be reused in other MCP servers over
REST: validation before writes, per-item results and batch semantics,
compensating rollback, version-checked partial updates (with the race
window that remains and the concurrency test results), and dry runs,
plus the measured before/after on the friction-report jobs.

The README now says what each new tool guarantees, including that the
batches are best-effort rather than all-or-nothing and the race window
the partial updates leave. src/tools/README.md points hand-written
tools at the shared primitives.

